From: LukeParkerDev <10430890+Hona@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:52:14 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(release): Linux engine probe proves start + page load,
 prints engine stderr on failure

- Engine stderr goes to a file; on any failure the probe prints the exit code, stderr tail, process tree (Seccomp/NoNewPrivs per process on Linux) and Chromium's debug.log tail.
- Linux renderers are found as the zygote's children (they keep --type=zygote in /proc/<pid>/cmdline).
- macOS renderers are found by the probe's own app bundle path (ps -axww), not by parent pid: run 44980898474's verify-engine-macos (x64) loaded the page but found no renderer whose parent was the engine.
- Renderer sandbox state is printed; it fails the check only with --require-sandbox, which macOS passes. Linux reports only until the Linux sandbox returns.
- The Linux engine archive is uploaded even when the probe fails.
